    <item>
      <title>Lecture 6: Graph Theory and Coloring</title>
      <link>https://tomodachii.com/courses/6.042j/lecture-6-graph-theory/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 02 Jun 2025 21:52:48 +0700</pubDate>
      <guid>https://tomodachii.com/courses/6.042j/lecture-6-graph-theory/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;definitions&#34;&gt;Definitions&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;graphs&#34;&gt;Graphs&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;$ G = (V, E) $&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;$ V $: &lt;strong&gt;non empty&lt;/strong&gt; set of vertices (or nodes)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;$ E $: edges; set of two-element subsets of $ V $.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;adjacent&#34;&gt;Adjacent&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Two nodes $ x_i $ and $ x_j $ are &lt;strong&gt;adjacent&lt;/strong&gt; if $ \{ x_i, x_j \} \in E $.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;incident&#34;&gt;Incident&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;An edge $ e = \{ x_i, x_j \} $ is &lt;strong&gt;incident&lt;/strong&gt; to $ x_i, x_j $.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;degree-of-a-node&#34;&gt;Degree of a Node&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The # of edges incident to a node.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Insertion Sort</title>
      <link>https://tomodachii.com/random/20240724-insertion-sort/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 24 Jul 2024 19:03:42 +0700</pubDate>
      <guid>https://tomodachii.com/random/20240724-insertion-sort/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;insertion-sort&#34;&gt;Insertion sort&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Insertion sort works the way you might sort a hand of playing cards&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Start with an empty left hand; all cards are in a pile on the table&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;With your right hand, pick up the first card in the pile&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Insert the card into the correct position in your left hand&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;pseudocode&#34;&gt;Pseudocode&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-html&#34; data-lang=&#34;html&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;INSERTION-SORT(A, n)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;1    for i = 2 to n&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;2        key = A[i]&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;3        // Insert A[i] into the sorted subarray A[1:i - 1]&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;4        j = i - 1&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;5        while j &amp;gt; 0 and A[j] &amp;gt; key&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;6            A[j + 1] = A[j]&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;7            j = j - 1&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;8        A[j + 1] = key&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Explain by a little example&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
